---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy notice"
  description="How Kilbride Electrical collects and uses enquiry and project information."
>
  <div class="page-head">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1 class="page-head__title">What we keep, and why.</h1>
    </div>
  </div>

  <article class="container prose">
    <p class="meta">Last reviewed 7 November 2026</p>

    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      Kilbride Electrical Contractors Limited, Unit 4, Mill Yard, Balheary, Swords, Co. Dublin,
      K67 X2R8, is the data controller for information sent through this site. You can contact us
      at <a href="mailto:estimating@kilbride-electrical.example">estimating@kilbride-electrical.example</a>
      or on <a href="tel:+35315550140">+353 1 555 0140</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The name, phone number, email address, site address and work description you send through the enquiry form.</li>
      <li>Project records created during a job: drawings, test results, certificates and correspondence.</li>
      <li>Standard server logs from our hosting provider, kept for security and fault diagnosis.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Why we use it</h2>
    <p>
      To answer your enquiry, prepare a quotation, deliver the work, issue certification and meet
      our statutory record-keeping duties. We rely on consent for the enquiry reply and on
      contract and legal obligation for project records. We do not sell personal data or use it
      for advertising.
    </p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      Enquiries that do not become jobs are deleted after 24 months. Project records, test
      certificates and safety documentation are kept for seven years after completion, or longer
      where a contract or insurer requires it.
    </p>

    <h2>Who sees it</h2>
    <p>
      Only staff who need it to answer the enquiry or run the job, plus our accountant, insurer and
      certification bodies where the law or the contract requires it. Our hosting provider stores
      the site and its logs within the European Economic Area.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
    <p>
      This site sets no advertising or analytics cookies. The enquiry form does not store anything
      in your browser. If a measurement tool is added later, this notice will say which one and
      what it records before it is enabled.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask for a copy of your data, ask us to correct or delete it, or withdraw consent for
      the enquiry reply. Write to the address above. If you are not satisfied, you can complain to
      the Data Protection Commission at
      <a href="https://www.dataprotection.ie" rel="noopener noreferrer">dataprotection.ie</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
